
.\" Manpage for quran-daemon
.TH QURAN-DAEMON 1 "Oct 2026" "v2.1.0" "Quran Player Daemon Manual"
.SH NAME
quran-daemon \- Quran Player Daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quran-daemon
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIARGUMENTS\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Quran Player Daemon is a Linux-native background service that provides
Quranic verse audio playback with synchronized desktop verse display via
Conky. It supports verse-by-verse playback with auto-advance, persistent
playback state across sessions, repeat ranges, an optional Conky desktop
overlay, and a PyQt5 tray GUI controller.

The daemon communicates with clients over a UNIX domain socket and is
configured via an INI-style configuration file.
.SH COMMANDS
The following commands are supported:
.TP
.B start
Start the daemon. Initializes audio, launches Conky (if enabled), binds the
control socket, and begins listening.
.TP
.B stop
Stop the daemon gracefully. Releases the audio device, terminates Conky, and
removes socket and PID files.
.TP
.B play
Resume audio playback from the last saved verse.
.TP
.B pause
Pause the current playback.
.TP
.B toggle
Toggle between play and pause.
.TP
.B next / prev
Advance to / return to the next / previous verse.
.TP
.B goto \fIayah\fR
Jump to a specific ayah in the current surah.
.TP
.B load \fIsurah\fR[:\fIayah\fR]
Load a surah from its beginning, or a specific verse.
.TP
.B repeat \fIform\fR
Set a repeat range (\fIsurah\fR, \fIstart:end\fR, or \fIsurah:start:end\fR).
Use \fBrepeat off\fR to disable.
.TP
.B repeat_off
Turn off repeat mode.
.TP
.B ns / ps
Next / previous surah. Clears any active repeat range.
.TP
.B dir \fIpath\fR
Change audio directory and reload the current verse.
.TP
.B conky_on / conky_off / conky_toggle
Start / stop / toggle the Conky desktop verse display.
.TP
.B conky_config / conky_config_defaults / conky_config_reset / conky_config_set
Inspect / show defaults / reset / validate-and-save the Conky display config.
.TP
.B config_get / config_defaults / config_set
Inspect / reset / validate-and-save config.ini.
.TP
.B reload_config
Re-read config.ini from disk and refresh daemon state.
.TP
.B status
Print a JSON status snapshot.
.TP
.B info
Print a detailed diagnostic report.
.TP
.B cleanup
Remove stale runtime files (PID, socket) when no daemon is running.
.TP
.B config
Regenerate the default configuration file.
.TP
.B about / help
Show project info and the full command reference.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The daemon uses an INI-style configuration file at:
.IP
\fB~/.config/quran-player/config.ini\fR
.PP
It has two sections: \fB[daemon]\fR and \fB[conky]\fR.
.SH "Daemon Section"
.TP
\fBmax_log_size\fR
Maximum size (in bytes) of the log file before rotation. Default: \fB1000000\fR.
.TP
\fBlog_level\fR
Log verbosity: \fBCRITICAL\fR, \fBERROR\fR, \fBWARNING\fR, \fBINFO\fR,
\fBDEBUG\fR, or \fBDISABLED\fR. Default: \fBINFO\fR.
.TP
\fBfiles_directory\fR
Directory containing audio files (\fISSSAAA.mp3\fR). Empty means use the
bundled sample directory \fB~/.config/quran-player/sample/\fR.
.SH "Conky Section"
.TP
\fBenable\fR
Show the current verse on the desktop via Conky (\fByes\fR / \fBno\fR).
Default: \fByes\fR.
.TP
\fBexecutable\fR
Path to the conky executable. Empty means auto-detect from \fBPATH\fR.
.SH "Conky Display Config"
Fine-grained Conky settings live in \fB~/.config/quran-player/conky_config.json\fR.
Edit via \fBconky_config_set\fR or the GUI's "Conky Config" dialog; invalid
JSON or schema violations are rejected before writing.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fBdaemon.py\fR
Main daemon entry point.
.TP
\fBquran_gui.py\fR
PyQt5 tray controller.
.TP
\fBquran_search.py\fR
Search tool (CLI and interactive).
.TP
\fBinstall.py\fR
Linux-native installer.
.TP
\fBdefault_config.ini\fR
Default configuration template.
.TP
\fBconfig.ini\fR
User configuration file (\fB~/.config/quran-player/config.ini\fR).
.TP
\fBconky_config.json\fR
User-editable Conky display config.
.TP
\fBdaemon.sock\fR
Control socket for inter-process communication.
.TP
\fBdaemon.pid\fR
Daemon process ID file.
.TP
\fBdaemon.log\fR
Daemon log file.
.SH USAGE EXAMPLES
.TP
Start the daemon:
.B
quran-daemon start
.TP
Stop the daemon:
.B
quran-daemon stop
.TP
Toggle playback:
.B
quran-daemon toggle
.TP
Load a specific verse:
.B
quran-daemon load 2:255
.TP
Repeat a range of verses:
.B
quran-daemon repeat 10:15
.TP
Display status:
.B
quran-daemon status
.TP
Generate a new configuration file:
.B
quran-daemon config
.TP
Display help:
.B
quran-daemon help
